{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "SzqxY",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Onboarding",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JlR5L",
          "name": "BriefTitle",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Onboarding — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VmXOS",
          "name": "BriefBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "First-run journey for the self-hosted single-user instance.\n\nEntry: root → /setup (no account yet) → onboarding wizard (integraciones → activos → seguridad → listo) → /welcome on first authenticated visit.\n\nScreens: Setup · Integrations · Assets · Seguridad · Complete · Welcome. Setup carries no Stepper because it is BEFORE the wizard — it creates the account; the four numbered steps start after it.\n\nRules: single user — no 'admin account' framing (D1-onb: reframe to 'tu cuenta'). Wizard steps skippable. Provider cards split keyed vs public (no key).\n\n✅ The wizard has FOUR steps, and Seguridad is the fourth (D52). ADR-018 builds TOTP with recovery codes and D52 put the ask in BOTH the wizard and Ajustes: the wizard OFFERS and lets you skip, Ajustes is where it is turned on later.\n\n⚠ The step OFFERS; it does not enrol. The QR, the one-time recovery-code display and recovery-code entry are three artboards in flows/auth.pen, and redrawing them here would be two files owning one flow. This screen is a card and two buttons: Activar ahora, or Ahora no · lo activo desde Ajustes.\n\nIt is step 3 of 4, not step 1, and the position is the decision. Recovery codes are shown ONCE. Put enrolment before the reader has configured anything and the ten codes they must not skim arrive on the screen they are most likely to rush; put it after integrations and assets and the codes land next to a wizard they have already invested in. Skippable either way, so the cost of being wrong is a click.\n\n✅ VOO and CETES are SPLIT, and this was not a design call — the code had already made it. This brief carried it as an open question: one card labelled 'ETFS · RENTA FIJA MX' put an S&P 500 equity ETF and Mexican government debt in the same box (C1 Lucía), and the fix was left unapplied 'because it changes the screen's shape'. Measured against config/locales/es-MX.yml: onboarding.categorias has FIVE entries and 'etfs' and 'fixed_income' are separate ones. The artboard was behind the code, the same shape D33 had in discover.pen. Now two cards, mobile and desktop.\n\n✅ The coherence flag against auth.pen is RESOLVED and was stale. This brief said 'Setup is a split-panel and Login is a plain centered card (420) … flagged rather than fixed — auth.pen was closed before this file was opened, and the two files cannot be edited in one session.' Measured: [Auth] / Login · Desktop is a 900 card = 420 Brand Panel + 480 Form Panel, the same split-panel as Setup. It was fixed in auth's own desktop pass and the note was never propagated back. The one-file-at-a-time rule was also over-read — it governs WRITING, because JSON merges badly; reading a second file to check a claim costs nothing.\n\n⚠ STILL OPEN, and it is a design call. The Brand Panel checklist mixes three wizard STEPS (conecta tus fuentes · elige los activos · lanza tu primer sync) with one CLAIM (100% libre y open source), and every item renders checked. In Setup that reads as a promise of what is coming; reused in the wizard it reads as 'all done' while you are on step 1, which is why the Stepper stays in the Form Panel. Two elements describe progress in the same view. Either the checklist gains state and drops the claim to its own line, or it stays a promise and the Stepper remains the only progress indicator. Note the checklist also names THREE steps against a wizard that now has four.\n\nThe ledger asked to 'check for a third OptionCard → NavRow consumer'. There is no OptionCard in this file — the item had no subject here.\n\nDesktop: Setup already had its split-panel (900 card = 420 brand + 480 form, the divergence D4 names). Integrations, Assets and Welcome join it. Complete and Seguridad are NOT drawn on desktop — both inherit the wizard frame exactly, so a second artboard would only restate it. Welcome sits outside that frame (post-wizard, no Stepper): a 900 centered column where the Guide's three cards sit SIDE BY SIDE. On mobile they are 444pt of scroll; the closed beta's first failure was 'I don't know what to do', and three doors seen at once beat three doors discovered by scrolling.\n\nCopy: es-MX (source screens are English — D2-onb). kit-version-source 0.9.0 — the brief claimed 0.1.0 against a variable reading 0.7.0, which makes it the EIGHTH brief of eight found contradicting its own file. Not one escaped. That is what D53 is parked about.\n\n✅ /help IS NOT DRAWN, AND THAT IS THE DECISION (D92). It is `/welcome` with the greeting swapped for a title and the CTA removed — same `shared/_welcome_body`, same container, same 900 max width. `design/README`'s own state rule covers it: build a state only when it carries information the design lacks, and a pure string swap goes in the brief. `Welcome / Default` already shows 95% of it, and two near-identical artboards are the drift that forces both to be maintained when one changes.\n\nWhat differs, in full: the greeting `Hola, {nombre}` becomes the title `Ayuda y soporte`, its subtitle changes, and the `Ver mi panorama` CTA at the foot is absent. Nothing else.\n\n⚠ The body's bug link opens the public issue tracker, not an in-app form: `/report-bug` was retired by D91. The artboard's copy reads `Ábrelo en GitHub.`",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
